  "body": "These are three separate commits that should probably be reviewed in order because of the way it has been done (mostly scripted, a few manual modifications when needed).\nI didn't do three PRs because of the potential conflicts that would have followed. I think squashing them will be the easiest solution.\n### style(require): Force extension for local requires\n\nIf `require` content starts with a dot, add `.js` to the `require`.\n\n``` sh\nag -l \"require\\([\\\"']\\.\" | xargs -I {} sed -i -r \"s#require\\([\\\"'](\\.[^\\\"']*/[^\\.\\\"']*)[\\\"']\\)#require('\\1.js')#g\" {} \n```\n\nFew manual modifications afterwards.\n### style(import): Use import over require at the root level\n\n``` sh\n# For `let xxx = require('xxx');`:\nag -l \"^let [a-zA-Z]+\\s*=.*require\\(['\\\"].*['\\\"]\\);$\" src/ | xargs -I {} sed -i -r \"s/^let ([a-zA-Z]+)\\s*=.*require\\(['\\\"]([^'\\\"]*)['\\\"]\\);$/import \\1 from '\\2';/g\" {}\n\n# For `require('xxx');`\nag -l \"^require\\(['\\\"].*['\\\"]\\);$\" src/ | xargs -I {} sed -i -r \"s/^require\\(['\\\"]([^'\\\"]*)['\\\"]\\);$/import '\\1';/g\" {}\n```\n### style(export): Use export default instead of module.exports …\n\n``` sh\nag -l 'module.exports =' index.js src | xargs -I {} sed -i -r 's/^module.exports =/export default/g' {}\n```\n\nSpecial treatment for `src/lib/version.js` which is generated and\nused in `scripts`, hence the update of\n`scripts/bump-package-version.js`.\n### Notes\n\nAs you might have noticed, the linter is now only passed on `index.js` and `src`. Scripts shouldn't rely on `node` understanding the ES6 syntax yet.\nThis has one drawback though : your editor will be screaming while editing js files in `scripts`. Not sure how to handle that. Maybe exclude them using `.eslintrc` ?\n\nAlso, I'm still unable to run `npm shrinkwrap`, hence the failing tests.\n",
